Technical Details
The architecture relies heavily on system calls provided by the <unistd.h> library:

fork() for process creation.

execvp() for replacing the child process image with the requested command.

pipe() for setting up unidirectional data channels.

dup2() for duplicating file descriptors to manage STDIN and STDOUT streams.

Known Limitations & Future Improvements
Built-in commands like cd are not currently supported as they require changing the parent process's state.

Spaces are strictly required around redirection and pipe operators (e.g., ls | wc works, ls|wc does not).

Signal handling (like Ctrl+C) currently exits the shell entirely rather than just terminating the running child process.
